From: Alex <05jeelo30@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:57:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Shift the system bars for burn-in protection

The framework burn-in protection only moves the display while it dozes,
so the status bar and navigation bar contents sit on the same pixels
the whole time the screen is on. Bring back the system bar shift from
Paranoid Android (kept alive by FlamingoOS and crDroid): every minute
while awake, move the status bar's start and end content and the
navigation bar contents (or the gesture handle) a few pixels.

It follows config_enableBurnInProtection, so it only runs on devices
that opt into burn-in protection. The controller watches wakefulness
itself, and the status bar and navigation bar view controllers hand it
their views on the default display.

